  AFAIK there is nothing so serious that can't wait for F-9 release. Also all 
modules need to be recompiled, this can be done best after F-9.

  Since the release schedule of R is 6 months I think that we should continue 
the policy, that has been followed, to release the new version as soon as 
feasible for all releases. This is different from the procedure used in perl, 
python, tcl but I think that in this case it is justified. Just my 2 ¢ (euro) 
on this issue. :-)
 
